@startuml project_components
title OpenCRM — application project layers

top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho

component "OpenCRM.WebApp\ncomposition root / HTTP host" as Web
component "OpenCRM.Modules.*\napplication modules" as Modules
component "Infrastructure.Auth / Admin / Payments / FileStorage" as Infrastructure
component "Services.Interfaces\nshared service contracts" as ServiceContracts
component "Modules.*.Contracts\nmodule service contracts and DTOs" as ModuleContracts
component "Infrastructure.Data\nEF Core / Identity" as Data
component "Domain.Interfaces\nrepository and unit-of-work abstractions" as DomainInterfaces
component "Domain\nentities and rules" as Domain

Web --> Infrastructure
Web --> Modules
Modules --> ServiceContracts
Modules --> ModuleContracts
Modules --> Data
Modules --> Domain
Infrastructure --> ServiceContracts
Infrastructure --> Data
Infrastructure --> Domain
Data --> DomainInterfaces
Data --> Domain
ServiceContracts --> ModuleContracts
ServiceContracts --> Domain
ModuleContracts --> Domain
DomainInterfaces --> Domain

note right of ServiceContracts
  Services.Interfaces references Domain and module contracts.
  It does not reference Infrastructure.Data or EF Core.
end note

note bottom of Web
  The WebApp wires the modules and infrastructure into one host.
  Payments.Service and Notifications.Worker are separate service projects.
end note

@enduml
